      "writtenOn": "2021-09-04T14:31:08Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "STOP_MASK assumes earlier we were in LIVESTREAM mode and stops it. \nIt doesn\u0027t bring device to known state, and actually bring it into odd state when I try to configure HW HMAC. In debugging why my HW HMAC produced wrong result I found that main difference from cr52 code is that the latter doesn\u0027t do it. So, I removed it first. But then I faced a bug which I introduced in case of 33-64 byte keys which resulted in attempt to set ONE-SHOT mode when LIVESTREAM was configured - state machine remained in an interesting state which led to wrong results. RESET_MASK however fixed this too (but didn\u0027t fix wrong results which were fixed by fixing root cause).\n \nRESET_MASK does soft reset of logic and brings device to known logical state, but doesn\u0027t clear secrets.  It seems better for reliability when different modes are used.",
      "parentUuid": "dfdcf742_9bbec1ec",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 113,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 113,
