      "writtenOn": "2021-09-04T14:31:08Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "for HMAC we deal with secret key, so adding stall cycles to better hide it. For SHA256 we typically process public data, so gain speed. Practically we only use 256-bit keys for all uses, so HMAC will use 25% cycles. HMAC DRBG 32-bit is impacted by 10% slowdown compared to 6%.",
      "parentUuid": "698668b4_a4e70bd1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 128,
        "startChar": 36,
